              "chapter": "Motion in a Straight Line",
              "exam_name": "NCERT Based",
              "question": "A graph of <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(x\\)</span> versus <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(t\\)</span> is shown in the figure. Choose correct alternatives from below.<br> <img src=\"https://d1rhszi3q7ul2h.cloudfront.net/s3buckets/neetprep-static-assets/question-assets/key__2024-07-25%2007%3A32%3A28%20%2B0000image.png\" style=\"width: 187px; height: 138px;\" />\r\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width:500px;\"><tbody><tr><td>(a)</td><td>The particle was released from rest at <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(t = 0\\)</span>.</td></tr><tr><td>(b)</td><td>At <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(B,\\)</span> the acceleration <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(a &gt; 0\\)</span>.</td></tr><tr><td>(c)</td><td>At <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(C,\\)</span> the velocity and the acceleration vanish.</td></tr><tr><td>(d)</td><td>Average velocity for the motion between <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(A\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(D\\)</span> is positive.</td></tr><tr><td>(e)</td><td>The speed at <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(D\\)</span> exceeds that at <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(E\\)</span>.</td></tr></tbody></table>Choose the correct option:\r\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\"><tbody><tr><td>1.</td><td>(b), (c), (d)</td><td>2.</td><td>(a), (b), (c), (d)</td></tr><tr><td>3.</td><td>(a), (d)</td><td>4.</td><td>(a), (c), (e)</td></tr></tbody></table>",
              "options": [
                "(1)",
                "(2)",
                "(3)",
                "(4)"
              ],
              "correct": 3,
              "explanation": "Hint:\\(a = \\frac{dv}{dt}\\)\n\nStep: Analyse each statement one by one.\nThe displacement time\\(x\\text-t\\)graph of the particle is given in question as;\n\nAt \\(t =0\\), the slope of the graph (which indicates velocity) appears to be\nzero, as the curve is flat. This suggests that the particle started from rest.\nSo, statement (a) is correct.\nAcceleration is the second derivative of \\(x\\) with respect to \\(t\\), or the\nconcavity of the curve. At point \\(B\\), the curve is concave downward,\nindicating a negative acceleration. So, statement (b) is incorrect.\nAt point\\(C\\), the slope of the curve (velocity) is zero, as it’s a turning\npoint. Additionally, since this point is an inflection point (where the curve\nchanges concavity), the acceleration also vanishes. So, statement (c) is\ncorrect.\nThe average velocity is the total displacement divided by the time taken.\nBetween points \\(A\\) and \\(D\\), the particle moves from a positive position to a\nzero position, resulting in a negative displacement. Therefore, the average\nvelocity would be negative. So, statement (d) is incorrect.\nSpeed is the magnitude of velocity. At point\\(D\\), the slope is steeper than at \n\\(E\\), indicating a higher speed at point\\(D\\).\nSo, statement (e) is correct.\nTherefore, the correct statements are (a), (c), and (e).\nHence, option (4) is the correct answer.<div style=\"margin-top:1.25rem; padding:0.85rem 1rem; background:var(--bg-secondary); border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:8px;\"><div style=\"display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:center; margin-bottom:0.6rem; font-weight:600; font-size:0.88rem;\"><span>📊 Student Attempt Analytics</span><span style=\"padding:2px 8px; border-radius:12px; font-size:0.75rem; font-weight:700; background:rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.15); color:#d97706;\">🟡 Medium · 49% Got This Correct</span></div><div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr); gap:0.5rem; text-align:center; font-size:0.82rem;\"><div style=\"padding:0.4rem; border-radius:6px; background:var(--bg-primary); border:1px solid var(--border);\"><div>(1)</div><div style=\"font-weight:700; margin-top:2px;\">14%</div></div><div style=\"padding:0.4rem; border-radius:6px; background:var(--bg-primary); border:1px solid var(--border);\"><div>(2)</div><div style=\"font-weight:700; margin-top:2px;\">17%</div></div><div style=\"padding:0.4rem; border-radius:6px; background:var(--bg-primary); border:1px solid var(--border);\"><div>(3)</div><div style=\"font-weight:700; margin-top:2px;\">22%</div></div><div style=\"padding:0.4rem; border-radius:6px; background:rgba(34,197,94,0.12); border:1.5px solid #22c55e;\"><div style=\"color:#16a34a; font-weight:700;\">(4) ✓</div><div style=\"font-weight:800; color:#16a34a; margin-top:2px;\">49%</div></div></div></div>",
